  "full_response": "Below is a sample JSON of a Postman collection export that includes environment variables for storing API keys, OAuth tokens, and basic authentication credentials. This collection setup demonstrates how you might structure a Postman project to manage and use secure credentials effectively.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"info\": {\n    \"_postman_id\": \"example-id\",\n    \"name\": \"API Sample Collection\",\n    \"schema\": \"https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json\"\n  },\n  \"item\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Get Example Data\",\n      \"request\": {\n        \"method\": \"GET\",\n        \"header\": [],\n        \"url\": {\n          \"auth\": {\n            \"basic\": [\n              \"{{username}}\",\n              \"{{password}}\"\n            ]\n          },\n          \"raw\": \"https://api.example.com/data\",\n          \"host\": [\n            \"api\",\n            \"example\",\n            \"com\"\n          ],\n          \"path\": [\n            \"data\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"description\": \"A request that uses basic authentication.\"\n      },\n      \"response\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Create Example Data\",\n      \"request\": {\n        \"method\": \"POST\",\n        \"header\": [\n          {\n            \"key\": \"Authorization\",\n            \"value\": \"Bearer {{oauthToken}}\",\n            \"type\": \"text\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"key\": \"Content-Type\",\n            \"value\": \"application/json\",\n            \"type\": \"text\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"url\": {\n          \"raw\": \"https://api.example.com/data\",\n          \"host\": [\n            \"api\",\n            \"example\",\n            \"com\"\n          ],\n          \"path\": [\n            \"data\"\n          ]\n        },\n        \"json\": {\n          \"name\": \"Sample Data\",\n          \"type\": \"Example\"\n        },\n        \"description\": \"A request that uses OAuth 2.0 Bearer token for authentication.\"\n      },\n      \"response\": []\n    }\n  ],\n  \"event\": []\n}\n```\n\n### Environment JSON\n\nHere’s how the corresponding environment might look where the variables `{{username}}`, `{{password}}`, and `{{oauthToken}}` are defined:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"example-environment-id\",\n  \"name\": \"API Development Environment\",\n  \"values\": [\n    {\n      \"key\": \"username\",\n      \"value\": \"your_username\",\n      \"enabled\": true\n   ",
